# Pin LF for text in the index AND the working tree.
#
# Without this, a tool that writes CRLF on Windows (PowerShell `Set-Content`
# and `Out-File` both default to it) leaves every file it touched showing as
# modified forever, with zero content difference. On 2026-09-06 this repo
# carried 506 modified roster HTML files -- 677,268 insertions against
# 677,268 deletions, and `git diff --ignore-all-space` was completely empty.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect and skip binary; `eol=lf` stops the checkout
# from re-introducing CRLF on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scraped payloads and columnar data are byte-exact. These are the bulk of
# the repo (~39k .gz, ~52 .parquet); mark them explicitly rather than relying
# on auto-detection alone.
*.gz      binary
*.parquet binary
